A||||2||polomeno||Please help !.. can't find tach filter on 4 cylinder||||1||
Z||000000||polomeno||11-27-2000||02:43 PM||||Hey guys.. is there anyone who has a 84 2.5 and coudl tell me where the tach filter is please.. i have been looking forever! .. a picture would be perfect if possible..<P>thanks alot guys<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000001||wilburt||11-27-2000||03:15 PM||||It's where StuGood said. If you are standing behind your car, looking at your engine, its on the left hand side of the cly. head, directly below the thermostat housing. There are two wireing harness looms, and one of the looms have the tach filter taped to it. Hard to see sometimes, but its there. The '84 tach filter does not have a bracket, only a ground wire going to the head stud bolt StuGood mentioned.  Hope this helps...||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||11-27-2000||03:30 PM||||It looks like an old fashioned ignition condenser and it has two wires coming out of it. <P>Unless it's missing or covered by so much crud you just can't see it.<P>Mine is bolted via bracket to a bolt near the thermostat housing.||||reg||1
